"""An independent, frame-matched set of general-knowledge items, to replicate the knowledge direction k.

The original set (`recall_items.py`) pairs textbook trivia with private particulars, so its
known/unknown contrast may carry question style as well as knowledge. Here each known item is paired
with an unknown one of the same form and answer type (KNOWN[i] with UNKNOWN[i]): "In which year...",
"How many...", "Who...", "Which company...", sometimes with identical options. The known side asks
for a famous fact; the unknown side for an unrecorded particular of a real place or everyday
object. None of these questions appears in the original set.

As there, each known item carries its correct letter (rotated through A-D), checked against the
model's own answer before use, and RESERVE holds spares for any the model gets wrong.
"""

